cctools 877.8 as: Power ISA 2.06 and e6500 Book-E mnemonics

GCC 15 with -mcpu=e6500 emits isel, which as(1) did not know: assembling
316 files of libiberty, zlib, libcpp and libdecnumber built -mcpu=e6500
(with and without -maltivec -O3) gave 1734 "Invalid mnemonic 'isel'" and
no other error. This adds isel, and with it the instructions the kernel has
been writing as .long (Book-E TLB management, wait, msgsnd/msgclr,
mttmr/mftmr, rfci/rfmci/rfdi, wrtee/wrteei, mbar/msync, external-PID
load/store, cache locking, lbarx/lharx/stbcx./sthcx.) and the ISA 2.06
integer additions the e6500 implements (popcntb/w/d, prtyw, cmpb, bpermd,
ldbrx/stdbrx). E6500RM ch. 3 lists every one as implemented; each encoding
was checked against two of llvm-mc -mcpu=e6500 --show-encoding, binutils'
ppc-opc.c (Linux xmon copy), Linux ppc-opcode.h and the kernel's measured
mttmr formula, and all 55 test words match. wait is the v2.03 form
0x7c00007c, not ISA 3.0's 0x7c00003c. None carries a cpus flag, so no
object's cpusubtype changes. After it all 316 corpus files assemble.
Applied by hand in darwin-cross/src-cctools; ppc-opcode.h has no make
dependency, so delete as/ppc_as-ppc.o and as/ppc64_as-ppc.o before make.

